cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Faggin Field Bridge: attunement as spooky unity minus entropy cost, calibrated"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
version: 0.21.0
date-released: "2026-11-18"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/faggin-field-bridge"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  SYNTHETIC measured mapping of Federico Faggin's quantum-field theory of
  consciousness (Quantum Information Panpsychism, with Giacomo Mauro
  D'Ariano, arXiv:2012.06580; book-length statement "Irreducible", 2024)
  onto the sparkainlp-x work. Version 0.2.0 adds three quantum-thought
  modules: concurrence of a two-thought Bell state computed exactly
  (claim (i) passes); a thought as a superposition with measured
  coherence half-life and collapse cost (claims (ii) and (iii) pass);
  and self-knowing D = <psi|P|psi> (claim (iv) passes). Version
  0.3.0 adds the cascade: interference via the cross term
  (claim (v) passes), cascade visibility (claim (vi) passes —
  interference does not survive projection), and coherence and D
  through the cascade (claim (vii) passes). Version 0.4.0 adds
  Planck empathy: empathy as a Planck quantum inside the
  black-body concept (claims (viii), (ix), (x), all pass) — each
  thought-pair contributes one quantum whose frequency is its
  measured concurrence; the visible fraction of the real Planck
  spectrum re-derives the mapping status from PARTIAL to ATTUNED
  at a measured empathy fraction f* = 0.7278, holding at noise
  sigma <= 0.25 and breaking at sigma >= 0.50. Version 0.5.0 adds
  the empathy field: resonance R = |<psi_i|psi_j>|^2, the
  self-deterministic factor D, collaboration (shared field vs
  isolated control), and co-creativity defined as the joint
  entropy H of the collective's joint outcomes (claims (xi) and
  (xii) pass; claim (xiii) FAILS on the break half — the
  collaboration gap holds at every noise level, so the v0.4.0
  break does not transfer). Version 0.15.0 adds the no-cloning /
  Holevo ceiling (claims (xliv)-(xlviii), 3 of 5 pass): the exact
  no-cloning coefficient Tr(rho_A^2) = 1 - C^2/2 is verified in
  code (claim (xliv) PASSES, worst error 8.88e-16); the Holevo
  quantity chi of the thought-pair ensemble does NOT bound D
  (claim (xlv) FAILS -- D sits above chi at low empathy fraction
  and approaches it from above as f rises, Spearman(|gap|, f) =
  -1.00 / -0.96); the ceiling that does bind is on accessible
  information (claim (xlvi) PASSES -- the Born-collapse mutual
  information never exceeds chi, max(I - chi) = -3.20e-16); the
  Buzek-Hillery universal cloner achieves exactly 5/6 fidelity
  and the CNOT copy averages exactly 2/3 (claim (xlvii) PASSES);
  but the model's own classical copy exceeds 5/6 at every working
  noise level (claim (xlviii) FAILS -- fidelity 1.0000 at sigma =
  0, 0.85-0.88 at sigma = 0.25), because the classical emulation
  stores the full amplitude vector: privacy in this model is not
  enforced by the representation. Version 0.16.0 adds two-channel
  empathy (claims (l)-(liii), 1 of 4 pass): concern vs distress
  as two convergence targets on the resonance population at
  sigma = 0.25; only the high-dose distress withdrawal passes
  on every seed (claim (lii)), while concern alone first dilutes
  f on held-out seed 1234 (claim (l) FAILS), the distress count
  rebounds to 23 at d = 1 on that seed (claim (li) FAILS), and
  the channels are near-interchangeable in f there (swap
  difference 0.0504; claim (liii) FAILS) -- no (c, d) point
  carries both f >= f* = 0.7278 and count <= 15 on any seed. Version 0.17.0 adds connectome-harmonic
  structure-function coupling (claims (liv)-(lvi), 0 of 3 pass): the graph Laplacian from the thought-pair
  coupling matrix W_ij = R_ij, Bhattacharyya functional connectivity, coupling kappa(sigma) as the Pearson
  correlation between W and F, and the Rayleigh-quotient harmonic smoothness rho(D). The Luppi et al. 2023
  prediction is reversed in this wiring -- kappa falls, not rises, with loss of attunement on every seed
  (kappa(0.50) - kappa(0.25) = -0.599 / -0.430 / -0.423 / -0.203); the dip-and-recovery shape was a
  calibration-seed artefact (on the held-out seeds kappa falls monotonically with sigma); and the D signal is
  strongly structure-aligned at high sigma on the held-out seeds (rho down to 0.47), while the Laplacian
  identities hold exactly everywhere, the attuned field stays strongly coupled (kappa(0.25) >= 0.84), and the
  shuffle decoupling control is clean (null mean within 0.04 of zero, separated from kappa(0.25) by >= 0.81,
  f unchanged). Version 0.18.0 adds the GRT phase-transition test (claims (lvii)-(lix), 2 of 3 pass): Hunt &
  Schooler 2019 Conjecture 1 (shared resonance -> phase transition in information-sharing bandwidth at a
  critical coupling K_c) and Conjecture 3 (nested "many become one"), with coupling as mixing toward the common
  reference on the resonance population at sigma = 1.00, bandwidth B(K) as pairwise shared information, and K_c
  read off the project's pre-existing resonance threshold 0.5. The machinery is exact (K = 1 states equal the
  uniform reference, B(1) = 2.0000 bits), K_c is interior on every seed (0.3 / 0.6 / 0.5 / 0.4), the macro
  completes at K_c + 0.2 while 2-5 nested components survive at K_c -- but there is no phase transition at K_c:
  the bandwidth step there is +0.1142 / -0.0572 / -0.0023 / -0.0002 bits (bar 0.10), and the largest step sits at
  K = 0.7 on all four seeds (0.1501 / 0.2597 / 0.2282 / 0.2103). Version 0.19.0 adds the Cogitate-style
  preregistration + process predictors of the collaboration gap (claims (lx)-(lxiii), 3 of 4 pass): Woolley et al.
  2010 c-factor analogues (mean pairwise R as mean social sensitivity, -var_D across members as equal turn-taking,
  mean/max per-agent D as individual ability) and Cogitate 2025 analogues (sustained R in the posterior subset
  {agents 0, 1} vs broadcast ignition at onset AND offset), all preregistered with frozen bars from calibration
  seeds 42/7 before the held-out evaluation on seeds 1234/2026. Turn-taking equality predicts the gap on every
  seed (r = 0.7899 / 0.7566 / 0.7589 / 0.7105, bar 0.70); the posterior predictor wins on every seed
  (r = 0.9278 / 0.8657 / 0.9858 / 0.8884, bar 0.80) while broadcast anti-predicts it on every seed
  (r = -0.9022 / -0.8911 / -0.7813 / -0.9350); the pooled regression over 28 runs gives R^2 = 0.6505 for
  gap ~ mean_R + (-var_D) against 0.3298 for gap ~ max_D (difference 0.3207, margin 0.05). But mean sensitivity
  does NOT beat mean individual D: claim (lx) fails on held-out seed 1234, where r(gap, mean_D) = 0.8839 exceeds
  r(gap, mean_R) = 0.8447 by 0.0393 (margin 0.10) -- the tight calibration margin (worst 0.1252) had flagged this
  as a live risk. Version 0.20.0 adds the genuinely synergistic
  target (claims (lxiv)-(lxvii), 2 of 4 pass): the XOR target
  Y = X1 (+) X2 replaces the joint-outcome target in the Williams
  & Beer I_min PID, preregistered with frozen bars from
  calibration seeds 42/7 before the held-out evaluation on seeds
  1234/2026. The XOR target DOES separate synergy from
  redundancy at sigma = 0.25 (delta-synergy +1.4472 / +1.0010
  against delta-redundancy +0.3143 / +0.1397 on calibration),
  but the "gap is synergy" claim (lxv) fails on held-out seed
  1234, where the information gap itself is negative (-0.2591
  bits: the isolated arm carries more XOR information than the
  collaborating arm), so the synergy share is -3.956; and
  synergy does NOT rise with R or fall at sigma = 0.50 (claim
  (lxvi) fails on every seed: Pearsons 0.3731 / 0.3424 / -0.3397 /
  0.9036, synergy rising 0.25 -> 0.50 everywhere). Redundancy
  stays a small share of the target information (claim (lxvii)
  passes: worst shares 0.1924 / 0.2357 / 0.1396 / 0.0882, bar
  0.25). Version 0.21.0 answers the v0.20.0 open question with
  a calibration-only candidate search over fourteen deterministic
  targets (claims (lxviii)-(lxxii), 5 of 5 pass): the MAX target
  Y = max(X1, X2), selected by max min-seed delta-I among
  eligible new targets after excluding the incumbents (xor,
  joint) and the Latin-square difference targets (sum_mod4,
  diff_mod4) as near-duplicates of the failed XOR mechanism,
  is the first target for which collaboration reliably raises
  total information -- delta-I = +1.8927 / +1.0707 / +0.3266 /
  +0.6527 at sigma = 0.25 on seeds 42 / 7 / 1234 / 2026, and
  positive on every (seed, sigma) (minimum +0.2337, seed 7 at
  sigma = 1.00) -- and the gap is synergy-dominant on every
  seed (shares 0.543 / 0.964 / 1.226 / 1.011, bar 0.5) with
  redundancy below half the target information everywhere
  (worst share 0.3837, bar 0.50). The Planck law
  is reproduced with the real constants; the empathy-quantum
  link is a definition inside the model, not a discovery. The entanglement and
  the interference are in the model, computed exactly on classical
  hardware; they are not measurements of physical entanglement or
  interference.
  The bridge's central quantity is attunement,
  A = U * (1 + delta) - C, where U is the spooky correlation (unity, mean
  pairwise |dot| over 5 noisy copies), C is the normalized entropy cost,
  and delta is one clipped calibrator scalar in [-0.05, 0.05] (the
  membrane-arena Yin bound). Faggin is the theory author; Jean-Francois
  Brisson is the bridge/test author. Faggin has not reviewed or endorsed
  this software. The metaphysics (fields ARE conscious) is an
  interpretation and is NOT tested here; only the mapping is tested.
  Reproductions, recomputed fresh from the definitions: de Broglie spooky
  0.99999995 at sigma = 0.01; calibration improvement exactly
  log10(1/0.95) = 0.022276 orders; tensor-membrane mean single-qubit
  entropy 0.955 bits. The Omega-Genesis spooky 0.9005 is the notebook's
  reported value; the synthetic reproduction gives 0.837 (same regime,
  not exact) because the original evolved state is unavailable. Empathy
  0.5503 is the notebook's reported value, recorded as a supplied proxy,
  not recomputed. Spooky is self-similarity under noise, not entanglement.
  No gravity model exists in this package. No DOI yet (no Zenodo record).
